## 3. GLOBAL INTERNATIONALIZATION (13 LANGUAGES, RTL, DYNAMIC TEXT & LOCAL FORMATS)
1. **Zero Hardcoded Strings:** NEVER write raw strings in UI, controllers, or error messages. All text must use generated localizations.
2. **Supported Languages (13 Languages):**
   - English (`en`), Chinese Mandarin (`zh`), Spanish (`es`), Portuguese (`pt`), German (`de`), French (`fr`), Italian (`it`), Japanese (`ja`), Korean (`ko`), Arabic (`ar`), Hindi (`hi`), Russian (`ru`), and Indonesian (`id`).
3. **Modular ARB Structure & RTL Support:** Separate `.arb` files for each language in `lib/core/l10n/arb/`. For RTL languages like Arabic (`ar`), enforce dynamic `TextDirection.rtl`, mirrored navigation, icons, progress bars, and container layouts via `Directionality`.
4. **Local Formats & Measurements:** Automatically adapt currency symbols (`$` vs `€`), date formats (`DD/MM/AAAA` vs `MM/DD/AAAA`), local time zones, and storage/performance measurement units according to the user's active locale.
5. **Dynamic Text Length (Flexible Layout):** Languages like German (`de`) or French (`fr`) can take up to **30% more horizontal/vertical space** than English. The UI must use flexible containers (`Flexible`, `Expanded`, `AutoSizeText`, `Wrap`, and responsive layouts) to prevent visual overflows or text clipping.
6. **Native Error Mapping & Hot-Switch:** Map C++/Rust error enums (`enum EmulatorErrorCode`) to localized ARB keys. Instant hot-switching between any of the 13 languages without restarting.

